# Google Ads & PPC

**Intent:** Launch and optimize Google Search campaigns for efficient CPA/ROAS — structure, keywords, RSAs, bidding. Skip for organic SEO (`on-page-seo.mdc`) or Meta/LinkedIn ads unless user expands scope.

## Pre-launch gate (do not spend until all checked)

- [ ] Conversion action defined + **value** assigned
- [ ] GAds ↔ GA4 linked; test conversion fired successfully
- [ ] Landing page loads **<3s** on mobile; message matches ad promise
- [ ] UTM parameters working
- [ ] Monthly budget and target CPA/ROAS documented

## Account structure

```
Account → Campaign (objective + budget) → Ad group (tight theme) → RSAs (max 3 per ad group)
```

**Naming:** `GOOG_[Objective]_[Theme/Offer]_[Date]` (e.g. `GOOG_Conv_Brand_FreeTrial_Ongoing`)

**Campaign types:**

| Type | When |
|------|------|
| Brand | Defend branded queries |
| Non-brand | High-intent solution keywords |
| Competitor | Trademark policy caution; separate budget |
| DSA | Only with strong negative keyword lists |

## Keywords and negatives

- Start **Exact + Phrase** for control; Broad only with Smart Bidding + robust negatives.
- Mine **Search Terms Report** weekly → add negatives + new keyword opportunities.
- When generating ad sets: **≥8 negative keywords** (campaign-level + ad-group-level).

## RSA spec (mandatory when generating ads)

**Hard limits per RSA:**

- **15 headlines**, each **≤30 characters** (show count: `Headline (28 chars)`)
- **4 descriptions**, each **≤90 characters**
- **2 paths**, each **≤15 characters**
- **Final URL:** https, matches landing page
- **Max 3 RSAs per ad group**

**Output order (prevents truncation):**

1. Ad group structure + keywords (match types)
2. Negative keywords (≥8)
3. Sitelinks (≥4), callouts (≥4), structured snippets if relevant
4. RSA1, RSA2, RSA3

## Optimization decision tree

| Symptom | Fix order |
|---------|-----------|
| CPA too high | Landing page → targeting → creative → Quality Score |
| CTR too low | New hooks/angles → audience fit → ad fatigue refresh |
| CPM high | Expand audience or improve relevance score |

Compare platform CPA to **blended GA4 CAC** — platform attribution is inflated.

## Bidding progression

1. Manual or cost cap while learning
2. After **50+ conversions** in 30 days → Target CPA or Target ROAS
3. Budget increases **20–30%** every 3–5 days max (avoid resetting learning)

## Retargeting (Google)

| Stage | Window | Message |
|-------|--------|---------|
| Hot | 1–7 days | Cart abandoners, trial starters — urgency, objection handling |
| Warm | 7–30 days | Pricing/feature visitors — social proof, demo |
| Cold | 30–90 days | Any visit — lighter touch |

**Exclude:** existing customers (unless upsell), recent converters (7–14 days), careers/support pages.

## Weekly review checklist

- [ ] Spend vs budget pacing
- [ ] CPA/ROAS vs target
- [ ] Search terms → new negatives
- [ ] Top/bottom ads by conversions
- [ ] Ad strength / frequency (fatigue?)
- [ ] Landing page conversion rate

## Common mistakes

- Spending without conversion tracking
- Too many campaigns (fragmented budget)
- Big bid/budget swings during learning phase
- Ad promise ≠ landing page H1

